  "name": null,
  "problem": "Find the shortest distance between the origin and the osculating plane for the curve $r(t)$ at the point where $t=0$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =({t}^{2}+\\sqrt{2})\\,i+(\\sqrt{2}-{t}^{2})\\,j+2t\\,k \\\\ T(0) & =k \\\\ N(0) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i-\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively.",
